From 9cc3beecebded4d35c5a2359f18a1b699dc11b6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <assistant@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 22:34:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add launcher icon: adaptive icon + legacy mipmaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Uses the provided detective-silhouette artwork as-is — no redesign,
only the technical work needed for Android launcher compatibility.

- mipmap-{m,h,x,xx,xxx}hdpi/ic_launcher.png: full-bleed square icon
  at 48/72/96/144/192px, for launchers that don't mask the icon.
- mipmap-{m,h,x,xx,xxx}hdpi/ic_launcher_round.png and
  .../ic_launcher_foreground.png: the same artwork scaled to 72% and
  centered on a black canvas (matching the artwork's own near-black
  background, sampled from its corners) so every silhouette and the
  magnifying glass stay inside the safe zone under a circular or
  squircle mask. Verified with a rendered circular-mask preview —
  the full-bleed version clips the outer two silhouettes' edges,
  the safe-zone version does not.
- mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml + ic_launcher_round.xml: adaptive
  icon (API 26+, which this app already requires via minSdk 26) with
  @color/ic_launcher_background (#000000, matching the artwork) and
  @mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground.
- colors.xml: added ic_launcher_background.
- AndroidManifest.xml: application now declares
  android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher" and
  android:roundIcon="@mipmap/ic_launcher_round".

No Java/game logic, strings, or other resources touched. Verified:
all new/edited XML is well-formed, every @mipmap/@color reference
resolves to an existing resource, and the existing Java sources still
compile cleanly (unchanged) against the same Android API stub set
used earlier in this project.
